        "body": "Serve Robotics Inc. /DE/ is a for-profit public company headquartered in San Carlos, California, trading under the ticker SERV. Its website describes the company as working on sustainable, self-driving delivery, asking why move a 2-pound burrito in a 2-ton car. The company presents itself as a low-emissions solution to the last-mile problem and says it sets the standard for safety on and beyond the sidewalk, protecting customer data, employees, and the public.\n\nThe site names a delivery robot called Saymo, which it says moonlights as John Mulaney's sidekick on the show \"Everybody's Live.\" The company also describes itself as a pop culture icon. No products are listed in the available data. The company has no litigation cases listed, and it has a California law exposure count of 281. It is registered with the SEC under CIK 0001832483.",
